{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Buon Natale: The Christmas Album felt like a natural choice because Christmas albums recur in my listening history.",
    "Its explicit Christmas theme gave me a clear connection to my past choices and enough reason to try it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Broadway cast recording and Bond collection did not connect to the Christmas listening that drew me to the one album I chose.",
    "Titles such as Greatest Hits and Take Me Home left me unsure of the musical connection, while The Perfect Gift only hinted at a holiday theme. That uncertainty was enough for me to pass."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seemed to stretch my interest in a few albums into an interest in a broad range of recordings, without a clear reason I would want each one.",
    "A gift-related title alone was too loose a connection to the explicitly Christmas-themed albums I had played."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several Christmas albums appeared close together in my history, making that shared theme a stronger connection than a generic album title.",
    "Those Christmas interactions were in late November 2014, while my latest interaction was in September 2016. Christmas music still interests me, but that older cluster does not establish what I want every visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The Christmas recommendation connected with a recurring interest, but most other choices gave me too little reason to engage."
}"}
